# The environment the harness needs, as an artifact rather than as a login shell.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Measured on GEX44, 2026-09-25: from a clean, non-login
# shell -- which is exactly what a systemd unit gets -- the harness does not run.
# Three independent reasons, none visible from an interactive session:
#
#   1. `mix` and `elixir` are NOT on the default PATH. They are mise shims, and
#      `env -i .../shims/elixir --version` answers
#      "mise ERROR elixir is not a valid shim". A shim resolves through a config
#      the unit does not carry, so a shim is not a path.
#   2. `mix run` aborts with "Mix requires the Hex package manager" ->
#      "Could not find an SCM for dependency :req", because MIX_HOME defaults to
#      $HOME/.mix and Hex actually lives under the mise install tree at
#      installs/elixir/1.17.3-otp-26/.mix/archives/hex-2.5.1.
#   3. Without a UTF-8 locale the VM warns it is "running with native name
#      encoding of latin1 which may cause Elixir to malfunction".
#
# So the unit carries the environment as a committed, hashed artifact. A shared
# profile is a variable with no changelog; this file is a variable with one.
#
# THE PATH IS PINNED TO THE OTP-26 BUILD ON PURPOSE. The OTP-27 Elixir that
# aborted the VM on install run 1 ("size_object: matchstate term not allowed
# (core dumped)") is STILL ON DISK at installs/elixir/1.17.3-otp-27. Anything
# that resolves Elixir by name rather than by path can still reach it. That is
# the whole reason HR-KEOSQ-01 says a precompiled artifact asserts MATCH and
# never a minimum.

HOME=/home/kobii
LANG=C.UTF-8
LC_ALL=C.UTF-8

# Exact binaries. Not the shims, not a version range, not $(which).
PATH=/home/kobii/keos/mise-data/installs/elixir/1.17.3-otp-26/bin:/home/kobii/keos/mise-data/installs/erlang/26.2.5.21/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

# The COMPILED tree. With ERL_LIBS the VM finds every built application, so no
# Mix, no Hex, no dependency resolution and no network are on the runtime path.
# Measured: apps start in 1.63 s and a full call to the pinned model returns in
# 2.41 s this way, against a `mix run` that does not start at all.
ERL_LIBS=/home/kobii/keos/keos_qwen_svc/_build/dev/lib

# Kept for the rare Mix invocation (a rebuild), pointing where Hex really is.
MIX_HOME=/home/kobii/keos/mise-data/installs/elixir/1.17.3-otp-26/.mix
MIX_ENV=dev

# The ledger's location is per-deployment by design and the unit is what sets
# it. KeosQwen.Provider says so in its own moduledoc: the destination is a
# compiled constant, the ledger root is not, and the property that makes the
# weaker one acceptable is that a UNIT sets it and a request cannot.
KEOS_QWEN_LEDGER_ROOT=/home/kobii/keos/ledger

KEOS_QWEN_ROOT=/home/kobii/keos
KEOS_QWEN_SVC=/home/kobii/keos/keos_qwen_svc
KEOS_QWEN_LEDGER_SCRIPT=/home/kobii/keos/keos_qwen/ledger/ledger.py
